{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"=== FIX IMPLEMENTED AND MUTATION-CHECKED. Gerrit 1232 (stacked on 1231, the diagnosis). ===\n\nTHE FIX, as proposed and signed off — plumb the canonical identity, do NOT relax the guard:\n  * `inbound_differ._diff_jira_vs_local:185-201` — when it emits an `assignee` change it now\n    also forwards `jira_mapped[\"assignee_identity\"]`. The mapper already computes it\n    (`inbound_fields:225`), so there is no new extraction, and `account_id` already holds the\n    accountId on Cloud and the username on DC (`_identity_of:154-179`, 5f48's precedence).\n  * `apply_inbound_records:374` — keys the mint on that identity,\n    `fields.get(\"assignee_identity\") or fields[\"assignee\"]`. The raw-object fallback keeps a\n    caller that BYPASSES the differ (still passing the Jira user object) byte-for-byte unchanged.\n  * `_ensure_inbound_assignee_identity:107-122` — reads `account_id` AFTER `accountId`/`name`,\n    and falls back to `display` for the human-readable name.\nThe `isinstance(assignee, dict)` guard is untouched. A bare string still mints nothing, and\nthat is now pinned by a test rather than being an accident.\n\nINERT FOR EVENT WRITING: `_inbound_update_write_edit_event` builds its EDIT from an explicit\nfield list (`_scalar_transforms`), so the extra key writes no extra ticket field. Verified by\nthe suites below, not by reading alone.\n\nRED -> GREEN AT BOTH BOUNDARIES (tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_inbound_update_assignee_mint_5200.py).\nBoth were seen RED before the fix, each naming its own mechanism:\n  * DIFFER — \"the inbound differ emitted an assignee change WITHOUT `assignee_identity`, so the\n    applier has only the scalar string to mint from and the mint no-ops (bug 8d68)\", with\n    `assert 'assignee_identity' in {'title': '', 'assignee': 'admin'}`.\n  * APPLIER — \"THE INBOUND UPDATE PATH MINTED NOTHING for jira/'admin' (bug 8d68): the applier\n    still keys the mint on the scalar assignee string, which\n    `_ensure_inbound_assignee_identity:105-106` rejects before reading any key\".\n  * CLOUD — \"the Cloud inbound update did not mint under the accountId '5b10a2844c20165700ede21g'\".\n(An earlier attempt failed with a TypeError from passing `tracker_dir` as a str — an INVALID red,\nproving nothing; it was fixed to a Path and re-run before the fix was written.) After the fix: 11\npassed across the two 5200 modules.\n\nCLOUD PROOF, which is the guard against the wrong fix. `test_the_cloud_update_path_keys_on_the_\naccount_id_not_the_display_name` drives the real differ + real applier phase with a Cloud-shaped\npayload ({accountId: 5b10a2844c20165700ede21g, displayName: \"Ada Lovelace\"}) and asserts BOTH\nthat the mint registers under the accountId AND that `resolve_mapping(\"jira\", \"Ada Lovelace\")`\nis None. A fix that made the mint accept a bare string passes on DC and FAILS here.\n\nMUTATION VERDICTS — two, each reverting one half, each failing for the right reason (all\nAssertionError; no AttributeError/ImportError):\n  * revert the DIFFER's forwarding -> 4 failed / 3 passed. Differ cell: \"the inbound differ\n    emitted an assignee change WITHOUT `assignee_identity`...\"; contract cell: \"the differ\n    forwarded None, which is not the mapper's canonical identity {'display': 'Administrator',\n    'email': 'admin@example.com', 'account_id': 'admin'}\"; both applier cells red downstream.\n  * revert the APPLIER's keying -> 2 failed / 5 passed, and the differ cell STAYS GREEN — the\n    two boundaries are independently pinned, so a regression names which half broke.\n\nONE EXISTING ASSERTION INVERTED, intent preserved and recorded in its docstring: the diagnosis\nmodule's `test_the_mapper_already_carries_everything_the_mint_needs` asserted\n`\"assignee_identity\" not in changed` to pin the DROP as the mechanism. It now asserts the\nforwarded value EQUALS the mapper's own canonical identity — same intent (\"the mint's input comes\nfrom the mapper, not from a re-derivation\"), stated positively. No other test changed.\n\nNO OTHER BEHAVIOUR MOVED: tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/{diffing,conflict,mutate} 676 passed;\ntests/integration/rebar_reconciler 35 passed; a full tests/unit + tests/integration run is in\nflight. `scripts/gen_env_registry.py` produces no diff (neither file reads env).\n\nMODULE SIZES: inbound_differ.py 706 -> 718; apply_inbound_records.py 565 -> 579. Both well under\nthe 800 cap.\n\nREMAINING: a live harness run to confirm J11's\n`test_the_inbound_assignee_mints_a_jira_family_identity` goes green with no assertion weakened."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785710267119917001,"uuid":"75274e40-f565-468e-b4aa-2c221bd10ab4"}